flowchart TB
    accTitle: When Renovate leaves a branch alone
    accDescr: Renovate compares the author and the committer of every commit on its branch with its own address and its rule gitIgnoredAuthors. A commit of Renovate lets it go on rebasing, and so does one of the fix bot, the branch bot or another bot, which commit as the release app: where Renovate runs as the release app, that is its own address, and for the Mend Renovate app the rules of the blueprint name it. A commit of anyone else, also a merge that a person starts with Update branch, counts as an edit, and Renovate leaves the branch alone until a person ticks the box in the pull request, which builds the branch anew without that commit.

    commit["A commit on a branch of Renovate"]
    who{{"`**Whose is it?**<br>Renovate compares its author and its committer`"}}
    own["Renovate's own address"]
    bots["The release app: the fix bot, the branch bot and the others<br>self and hub: Renovate's own address<br>mend: the rule gitIgnoredAuthors of the blueprint"]
    person(["Anyone else,<br>also a person's Update branch"])
    rebases["Renovate goes on rebasing and updating the branch"]
    edited["Renovate takes it for an edit and leaves the branch alone"]
    box(["A person ticks the box in the pull request"])

    commit --> who
    who --> own & bots & person
    own & bots --> rebases
    person --> edited --> box
    box -- "the branch is built anew, without that commit" --> rebases

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class commit,who,own,bots bot
    class person,edited,box person
    class rebases done
